      <activity id="ae764649-6d87-5f40-ae81-285966a46f2f" activityNameId="729c8333-4f47-5c00-9a2c-1b4e71ac1580" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Electricity, residential, by combustion of hydrogen using CHP, allocated by exergy, distributed by pipeline [d007fa72dc]</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Electricity, residential, by combustion of hydrogen using CHP, allocated by exergy, distributed by pipeline, produced by Electrolysis, SOEC using electricity from grid
This dataset represents the supply of 1 kilowatt hour of electricity in a residence, by hydrogen combustion in a CHP. The hydrogen is produced by  Electrolysis, SOEC, with electricity from grid as feedstock. Electricity conversion efficiency [% LHV input]: 39.4%. LHV [kWh/kg]: 33.33. Market price [Euro/MJ]: 0.03. Synthesis efficiency [% LHV input]: 0%. Total cap. Input-related [kW]: 443.9. CO2 biogenic share [%]: 0%. Power [kW]: 200. Lifetime [years]: 19.51. Annual operation [hours]: 4100. Allocation factor: 0.92. On-site storage loss [%]: 0. Use loss [%]: 0.5. For more information, refer to: Sacchi, R. and Bauer, C. LCA of Power-to-X processes and applications in the residential sector. Paul Scherrer Institut, 2023. Source: Sacchi, R. and Bauer, C. LCA of Power-to-X processes and applications in the residential sector. Paul Scherrer Institut, 2023.

 UUID: 9beda5cc-287f-3bd7-9299-1f399acc5332
Location: 
Technology: 
Time period: 
Production volume: 
Sampling: Sampling procedure: Literature data
Extrapolations: 
Uncertainty adjustments: 
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_9beda5cc-287f-3bd7-9299-1f399acc5332.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
